{"title":"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A chord which is the perpendicular bisector of a radius of length 12 in a circle, has length \n</p><p>\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f15ed027f185de4cea16a7a5ba9c883f94ac979.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3\\sqrt3\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 27\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 6\\sqrt3\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 12\\sqrt3\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{ none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"531\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/1/5811cf5242e0d777fab9f039e8a3153791f6adc4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  draw(circle((0,0),12)); draw((0,0)--(0,12)); draw((0,0)--(10.392,6)--(-10.392,6)--(0,0)); label(&quot;$12$&quot;,(5.196,3),SE); label(&quot;$12$&quot;,(-5.196,3),SW); label(&quot;$6$&quot;,(0,3),E); draw((1,6)--(1,5)--(0,5));  [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>Draw a diagram as shown.  Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> (or by using 30-60-90 triangles), half of the chord length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/8772d61f5af0b70f355caf61084162db9b47f34b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />, so the chord’s length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/c/78cc9993f131477af56f2554684289461ef31c45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 12\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"90\" height=\"33\" />.  One can also find the length directly by using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME\" title=\"1973 AHSME\">1973 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1973 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1973\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/w